From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Pfeiffer <cpfeiffer@rev-crew.info>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:43:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Fix the values of x86_64 Windows DHooks params in
 registers

On x86_64 Windows, DHookParam.Get of a dynamic detour returns garbage
for every param passed in a register, i.e. the first four arguments.
x86_64MicrosoftDefault assigns RCX, RDX, R8 and R9 (XMM0 to XMM3 for
floats) to them itself, and GetParamStruct saves their values after
the stack arguments in the parameter buffer, but the setup's params
never learnt their registers: their custom_register stayed None, so
GetParamOffset took them for stack arguments and read them from the
start of the buffer, a copy of the stack.

Give the params the registers that the calling convention assigned, in
UpdateRegisterArgumentSizes, next to their sizes. With that,
GetRegisterParamOffset finds them after the stack arguments, which it
then has to count as GetParamStruct copied them: the 32 bytes of shadow
space first (x86_64MicrosoftDefault::GetArgStackSize), then 8 bytes per
stack argument, as GetStackParamOffset already does on x86_64.

Builds on the previous patch, of thiscall detours without params, which
fixes the indices of the params in UpdateRegisterArgumentSizes.

Tested with Day of Infamy's 64-bit Windows server (srcds_x64):
- Under Wine (wine-cachyos 10.0), DHooks built with clang-cl and xwin's
  MSVC libraries: a post detour of
  CINSRules::GetTotalActivePlayersOnTeam(int) reads team for a call
  with 3 as -1072758784 with master, as 3 with this patch. A second
  setup of the same function needs the patch of params of a second
  setup as well.
- On Windows 11, built with MSVC 14.52 (Visual Studio 2026), the param
  read 3 already with the previous patch alone: what the wrong register
  holds differs between clang-cl's and MSVC's builds, so the bug
  doesn't show there with this test. With this patch, it reads 3 there
  as well.

With the five DHooks patches, nwi_gamedata's detours of Day of Infamy's
game rules (doi-config) let bots play coop and PvP rounds on the 64-bit
Windows server as on 32-bit.
---
 extensions/dhooks/dynhooks_sourcepawn.cpp | 3 +++
 extensions/dhooks/util.cpp                | 9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/extensions/dhooks/dynhooks_sourcepawn.cpp b/extensions/dhooks/dynhooks_sourcepawn.cpp
index 970eeaa2..9885e2e8 100644
--- a/extensions/dhooks/dynhooks_sourcepawn.cpp
+++ b/extensions/dhooks/dynhooks_sourcepawn.cpp
@@ -330,6 +330,9 @@ bool UpdateRegisterArgumentSizes(CHook* pDetour, HookSetup *setup)
 
 		argTypes[i].size = reg->m_iSize;
 		setup->params[i - firstArg].size = reg->m_iSize;
+		// The calling convention assigns the registers of the params on x86_64, which the params need
+		// to find their values (GetParamOffset).
+		setup->params[i - firstArg].custom_register = argTypes[i].custom_register;
 	}
 
 	return true;
diff --git a/extensions/dhooks/util.cpp b/extensions/dhooks/util.cpp
index ac9b678a..915b29f0 100644
--- a/extensions/dhooks/util.cpp
+++ b/extensions/dhooks/util.cpp
@@ -78,11 +78,20 @@ size_t GetRegisterParamOffset(HookParamsStruct *paramStruct, unsigned int index)
 
 	// Need to get the size of the stack arguments first. Register arguments are stored after them in the buffer.
 	size_t stackSize = 0;
+#if defined(KE_ARCH_X64) && defined(WIN32)
+	// The 32 bytes of shadow space, which GetParamStruct copies with the stack arguments
+	// (x86_64MicrosoftDefault::GetArgStackSize)
+	stackSize = 32;
+#endif
 	for (int i = paramStruct->dg->params.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--)
 	{
 		if (paramStruct->dg->params[i].custom_register == None)
 		{
+#ifdef KE_ARCH_X64
+			stackSize += 8;
+#else
 			stackSize += paramStruct->dg->params[i].size;
+#endif
 		}
 	}
 
